.SH SHADERBG(1)
.SS NAME
shaderbg \- Shader wallpaper utility for Wayland
.SS SYNOPSIS
\f[B]shaderbg\f[R] OPTIONS [FILE]
.PP
\f[B]shaderbg\f[R] [\f[B]\-h\f[R]|\f[B]\(enhelp\f[R]] \f[B]shaderbg\f[R]
[\f[B]\-V\f[R]|\f[B]\(enversion\f[R]]
.SS DESCRIPTION
\f[B]shaderbg\f[R] renders shaders as live wallpapers in Wayland
compositors that support the wlr\-layer\-shell protocol.
Shaders can be loaded from preset files or imported from ShaderToy JSON
exports.
.SS ARGUMENTS
.TP
\f[I]FILE\f[R]
Optional path to a TOML preset file or ShaderToy JSON export file
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\(enno\-overlay\f[R]
Disable the shader information overlay display
.TP
\f[B]\(enexclusive\-zone\f[R] \f[I]ZONE\f[R]
Override the layer\-shell exclusive zone of the render window.
Default is \-1, or 0 on River
.TP
\f[B]\(eninput\-layer\f[R] \f[I]LAYER\f[R]
Layer of the input\-capture window: background, bottom, top, or overlay.
Default is background, or bottom on COSMIC.
Only has an effect when input passthrough is disabled
.TP
\f[B]\-h\f[R], \f[B]\(enhelp\f[R]
Print help information and exit
.TP
\f[B]\-V\f[R], \f[B]\(enversion\f[R]
Print version information and exit
.SS FILES
.TP
\f[B]\(ti/.local/share/shaderbg/assets/\f[R]
Default directory for assets (ShaderToy predefined textures)
.TP
\f[B]\(ti/.local/share/shaderbg/presets/\f[R]
Directory containing preset files
.SS EXAMPLES
.TP
\f[B]shaderbg\f[R]
Start with a random shader preset
.TP
\f[B]shaderbg \(ti/.local/share/shaderbg/presets/galaxy.toml\f[R]
Load a specific shader preset
.TP
\f[B]shaderbg shadertoy\-export.json\f[R]
Import from ShaderToy JSON export file
.TP
\f[B]shaderbg my\-shader.toml \(enno\-overlay\f[R]
Load preset without displaying the shader information overlay
.TP
\f[B]shaderbg \(eninput\-layer bottom\f[R]
Run the input\-capture window on the bottom layer instead of the default
for the current compositor
.SS ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\f[B]XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP\f[R]
Used to auto\-detect compositor\-specific defaults (exclusive zone 0 on
River, input window on the bottom layer on COSMIC)
.PP
The application may use standard XDG environment variables for
configuration directory location.
.SS NOTES
This utility requires OpenGL 4.2+ and a Wayland compositor with
wlr\-layer\-shell support.
